 "summary": "Marks files opened through fsbridge::fopen as non-inheritable and close-on-exec across platforms. It appends the 'e' mode specifier on Linux, appends 'N' on Windows, and implements an open() fallback with O_CLOEXEC followed by fdopen() for other POSIX operating systems like macOS and BSD. A unit test is included to assert that opened files lack the inheritance flag.",
 "problem": "File descriptors and handles opened through fsbridge::fopen remain inheritable across process boundaries by default, risking descriptor leaks into child processes executed by Bitcoin Core (such as external signers or notification scripts).",
 "evidence": [
  "Addresses issue #36668 ('util: Make files opened via `fsbridge::fopen()` not inheritable by child processes')."
 ],
